{{!
    @template tool_vae/selfpos_records

    The records the vaeiste may position themselves on: the two sentences of every screen, a notice for each record that is
    hidden, then the sentence that asks to choose and the list of the records, or the sentence that there is none.

    Every text comes from the context, already worded by tool_vae\output\selfpos_records. The template holds no logic. Every
    value is escaped (double braces) except two keys:
    * disclaimerhtml - the two sentences, drawn by the template tool_vae/selfpos_disclaimer
    * messagehtml - the message of a hidden record, a sentence of the language file whose title of the record was escaped
      by hidden_frameworks::message() (s()): placed as it is, as before, so that the title is escaped once

    Classes required for JS:
    * none

    Data attributes required for JS:
    * none

    Context variables required for this template:
    * disclaimerhtml - string, HTML of a template
    * hidden - array of {messagehtml}
    * none - object or null: text, the sentence said when no record is offered
    * list - object or null: choose (the sentence above the list), items (array of {url, code})

    Example context (json):
    {
        "disclaimerhtml": "<p class=\"text-muted small tool-vae-selfpos-disclaimer\">This is not a validation.</p>",
        "hidden": [{"messagehtml": "The record Aide &amp; soins (RNCP100) is hidden."}],
        "none": null,
        "list": {
            "choose": "Choose a certification record",
            "items": [{"url": "https://example.com/admin/tool/vae/selfposition.php?userid=7&fiche=RNCP400", "code": "RNCP400"}]
        }
    }
}}
{{{disclaimerhtml}}}{{#hidden}}<div class="alert alert-info">{{{messagehtml}}}</div>{{/hidden}}{{!
}}{{#none}}<p class="text-muted">{{text}}</p>{{/none}}{{!
}}{{#list}}<p>{{choose}}</p><ul>{{#items}}<li><a href="{{url}}">{{code}}</a></li>{{/items}}</ul>{{/list}}
